<title>USA: First Empire Q3 diluted shr rises to $5.05.</title>
<headline>First Empire Q3 diluted shr rises to $5.05.</headline>
<dateline>BUFFALO, N.Y. 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months ended Sep 30</p>
<p>						   1996	1995  Change</p>
<p> Net interest income			$132,201  123,865    7%</p>
<p>Less:  Provision for possible</p>
<p>   credit losses				10,475   11,310   (7)</p>
<p>Gain (loss) on sales of bank</p>
<p>   investment securities			(15)    4,933 (100)</p>
<p> Other income				   44,908   39,465    14</p>
<p> Net income				     35,871   35,627    1%</p>
<p> Taxable-equiv net interest income    133,452  125,045    7%</p>
<p> Dividends on preferred stock		  --	900 (100%)</p>
<p>Per common share:</p>
<p>Net income</p>
<p>     Primary					5.05     5.14  (2%)</p>
<p>     Fully diluted				5.05     4.89     3</p>
<p>Net income excluding securities transactions</p>
<p>   Primary					  5.05     4.71     7</p>
<p>   Fully diluted				  5.05     4.50    12</p>
<p>Common shares outstanding:</p>
<p>   Average(A)				    7,104    6,763    5%</p>
<p> Net interest margin(B)			4.38%    4.35%</p>
<p>						 Nine months ended Sept 30</p>
<p>						    1996     1995  Change</p>
<p> Net interest income			 $394,400  361,469   9%</p>
<p>Less:  Provision for possible</p>
<p>   credit losses				 31,850   28,325   12</p>
<p>Gain (loss) on sales of bank</p>
<p>   investment securities			  412    4,887 (92)</p>
<p> Other income				   122,195   99,801   22</p>
<p> Net income				     110,683   94,249  17%</p>
<p> Taxable-equiv net interest income	397,658  365,088   9%</p>
<p> Dividends on preferred stock		  900    2,700 (67%)</p>
<p>Per share net income:</p>
<p>     Primary					15.61    13.50  16%</p>
<p>     Fully diluted				15.36    12.83   20</p>
<p>Net income excluding securities transactions</p>
<p>   Primary					  15.58    13.08   19</p>
<p>   Fully diluted				  15.33    12.44   23</p>
<p>Common shares outstanding:</p>
<p>   Average(A)				     7,032    6,783   4%</p>
<p>(A) -- Includes common stock equivalents</p>
<p>(B) -- On a fully taxable-equivalent basis  </p>
<p>NOTE: Third quarter includes an after-tax charge of $4.1 million, or $0.58 per share, for a special assesment to recapitalize the Savings Association Insurance Fund.</p>
<p>Loans due past 90 days or more and accruing interest totaled $37 million on September 30, up from $16.5 million in the year-ago period. The increase was mainly due to inclusion of $17.5 million of residential mortgage loans First Empire serviced and purchased from the Government National Mortgage Association.</p>
<p>Full company name is First Empire State Corp.  </p>
<p>The company also reported that its total nonperforming loans were $96.5 million on September 30 this year, compared with $76.2 million for the 1995 period ending September 30.</p>
